BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 677.0 Tm (FAT32 traded more allocation-table space and more complex reserved-sector metadata for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 660.0 Tm (reduced cluster sizes on large disks. It preserved compatibility with short DOS names and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 643.0 Tm (removable-media firmware, but retained linear chains and the potential performance cost of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 626.0 Tm (severe fragmentation. Standard FAT directory entries encode a 32-bit file size, yielding) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 609.0 Tm (the familiar under-4-GiB single-file ceiling.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 580.0 Tm (FAT32 does not encode Unix permissions, native transactional snapshots, hard-link reference) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 563.0 Tm (counts or cryptographic integrity. This simplicity is an advantage for interoperable) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 546.0 Tm (firmware and media tools while placing the burden of durable writes and repair on operating) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 529.0 Tm (systems and external utilities.) Tj ET
